INT. DERELICT ORBITAL STATION - OBSERVATION RING - CONTINUOUS

Frost on the viewport. Beyond it, a gas giant fills the sky, banded and indifferent. Emergency lights pulse amber.

ORSOLYA, 40s, scavenger's patched suit, helmet clipped to her hip, drifts along a handrail. TAVI, 20s, tool belt too big for him, follows with a lantern.

She stops. Taps the wall. Listens.

ORSOLYA
(to the empty ring)
Anyone aboard. We're salvage. We mean no harm.

Silence. Frost ticks on the glass.

TAVI
Maybe just--

She raises a hand. He stops.

ORSOLYA
(again, louder)
Anyone aboard.

A pause. Nothing. She nods once, as if she expected nothing.

She opens a wall panel. Wiring shredded. Burned.

ORSOLYA (CONT'D)
(muttering)
Not an accident.

TAVI
What?

ORSOLYA
Nothing. Hold the light.

He holds it. His hand trembles. The beam shakes across the wires.

She notices. Says nothing. Takes the lantern from him. Hands him a screwdriver instead.

ORSOLYA (CONT'D)
Twelve screws. Take the plate off.

He works. Slowly. His eyes keep sliding to the viewport.

A thud rolls through the ring. Metal on metal, somewhere aft.

Both freeze.

TAVI
That was close.

ORSOLYA
That was far.

TAVI
It sounded close.

ORSOLYA
Far things sound close in a hull.

She doesn't sound sure. Her thumb strokes the edge of the lantern.

The thud again. Louder. Then a long scrape.

Tavi drops the screwdriver. It floats, tumbling.

ORSOLYA (CONT'D)
(to the ring, calm)
Everyone stay where you are. This is a recovery crew. We're leaving in five minutes.

TAVI
There's no one here.

ORSOLYA
I know.

She grabs his sleeve. Tows him toward the airlock. Her grip is gentle. Too gentle.

They reach the hatch. She spins the wheel. It opens onto the cold, bright tunnel of their own ship.

She pushes him through first.

TAVI
(over his shoulder)
You okay?

ORSOLYA
Fine.

She follows. Looks back once. The ring is quiet, amber, still.

Then, from the dark, one more knock. Small. Almost polite.

She seals the hatch.

ORSOLYA (CONT'D)
(to herself)
Five minutes.

She doesn't move for a long time. Tavi picks up the lantern and sets it between them, lighting both their faces.
